# 18. Scheduling Engine

This is the most important technical part of the product.

The engine must:

1. Cover exactly Juz 1 through Juz 30 every week.
2. Assign exactly 30 Juz worth of reading every week.
3. Respect each member's weekly Juz amount.
4. Never assign a member Quran material outside their knowledge range.
5. Change assignments between weeks whenever mathematically possible.
6. Avoid giving the same member the same Juz repeatedly.
7. Keep the distribution sequential where possible.
8. Support partial Juz boundaries when required.
9. Calculate exact starting ayah.
10. Calculate exact ending ayah.
11. Produce deterministic results for the same input.
12. Validate the generated schedule before displaying it.

The generated schedule must pass an internal validation step.

Validation must confirm:

Total assigned reading = 30 Juz.

All Quran coverage from Juz 1 through Juz 30 is covered.

No overlapping assignments.

No uncovered sections.

Every member receives their required weekly amount.

Every assignment is inside the member's allowed Quran range.

All start and end Quran references are valid.

If validation fails, do not display a broken schedule.

Return a clear error state.

